# auto-changelog — Project Rules

## What this project is
AI-powered changelog generator for GitHub repos. Backend is Python/FastAPI (async SQLAlchemy), frontend is pre-built React+Vite in `frontend/dist/` (source is NOT in this repo — never try to "fix" frontend source that doesn't exist here).

## Stack & Commands
- Python 3.12+, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2.0 async, aiosqlite (dev) / asyncpg (prod), Pydantic v2, python-jose, GitPython
- Run backend: `cd backend && source venv/bin/activate && uvicorn app.main:app --port 8003 --reload`
- Tests: `cd backend && source venv/bin/activate && pytest tests/ -v` (pytest + pytest-asyncio, use httpx TestClient)
- Migrations: Alembic (`backend/alembic/`)
- Frontend: already built in `frontend/dist/` — only rebuild with Node if explicitly asked

## Code conventions
- All DB operations async (`AsyncSession`, `selectinload`, etc.) — never write blocking DB calls
- Config lives in `backend/app/config.py` (Pydantic settings) — read values from `backend/.env`, never hardcode secrets
- Routers in `app/api/`, business logic in `app/services/`, background jobs in `app/tasks/`, Pydantic models in `app/schemas/`, SQLAlchemy models in `app/models/`
- Follow conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`) — this repo's changelog tooling depends on it

## Security — CRITICAL
- Never commit or print: `.pem` private keys, `.env` contents, OAuth secrets, API keys
- `*.pem`, `*private-key*` are gitignored — keep them that way
- Don't log token/session payloads

## When doing work here
- Run existing tests after backend changes; add tests for new endpoints/services
- LLM provider code: keep provider-agnostic — changes must work across OpenAI/Anthropic/Groq/OpenRouter/Ollama/commit-based mode
- Webhook handling must stay idempotent (GitHub retries deliveries)

## Memory bank (`.cline/memory-bank/`)
- At the START of a non-trivial task: read `projectbrief.md`, `activeContext.md`, and `progress.md`
- At the END of a completed task: update `activeContext.md` (current focus, issues) and `progress.md` (what was done)

